orbitra-bluespace-hint-off = Press "Enable" once the device is anchored and connected.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-unanchored = Secure the device with a wrench, then connect the power.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-no-station = Place the device on a station floor tile.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-no-power = Check the cable connection and available network power. Probers and suppressors require almost their full requested power.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-no-server = Link a powered research server on this station.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-critical = Activate suppressors. Reduce the shared background below 80, then restart the device.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-blocked = Clear a floor tile 2–3 tiles from the harvester. The batch is waiting to be released.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-working-harvester = Energy is accumulating for a batch. Partial power makes harvesting slower.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-working-harvester-overdrive = Overdrive accumulates energy and raises station instability faster. Watch the shared background.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-working-prober = Points are sent to the linked research server. Watch the shared station background.
orbitra-bluespace-hint-working-suppressor = The suppressor lowers the station's shared background and continues during an emergency shutdown.
orbitra-bluespace-effect-prober = Produces research points and raises the shared station background. Multiple probers have diminishing returns.
orbitra-bluespace-effect-suppressor = Stabilizes the station's bluespace field. After an emergency, the background must drop below 80 before harvesting and research can resume.
orbitra-bluespace-effect-paused = The effect is paused until the cause above is resolved.
